      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b46b03e_91f72699",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NattSocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-07T18:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we actually need a start method? RAII seems like a much tidier pattern, and it makes things like try-with-resources work as intended. Then people can do things like:\n\ntry (NattSocketKeepalive \u003d new NattSocketKeepalive(...)) {\n    // go to sleep here.\n    while(!recv(longTimeout)) {\n        doDpd();\n    }\n} except (DpdException dpdE) {\n    log(\"something went wrong\");\n}",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e310086_a0519edf",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NattSocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-07T18:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the looper isn\u0027t directly used by this class, it\u0027s odd to have the error condition here stop the looper. Is there a way to refactor so that this class doesn\u0027t deal with the looper?\n\nSide note: the entire thread isn\u0027t needed anyway. You can either remove it entirely and use the binder thread or (less good) use the ConnectivityManager thread.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
