        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 60,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40307fdc_d229593e",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/SocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-07T18:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can we ditch the looper, the messenger and the whole lot? The wonderful thing about the Executor is that the user specifies the context on which their code is executed. It\u0027s fine for the post to happen on the Binder thread.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9eb6f77c_efe53359",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/SocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-07T18:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unless we are going to support TCP, we should probably not confuse things. Besides, AIUI, \"protocol-specific\" info will be in a subclass specific to TCP at some point in the future, no? Also, does this method need to be public? I know the implementations need to be public, but ISTM this could remain @hide?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
